<title>HONG KONG: HORSE RACING-RESULTS FROM MAJOR RACES AT SHA TIN.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS FROM MAJOR RACES AT SHA TIN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on Sunday of  major</p>
<p>international horse races at Sha Tin:</p>
<p>Hong Kong International Cup, for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards run over nine furlongs (1.8 km)</p>
<p>1. First Island (ridden by M.Hills)</p>
<p>2. Seascay (D. Oliver)</p>
<p>3. Kingston Bay (P. Tims)</p>
<p>12 ran. Winning distances: three quarters of a length, half</p>
<p>a length.</p>
<p>Winner trained at Newmarket in England by Geoffrey Wragg and</p>
<p>owned by Moller Racing.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: $487,700</p>
<p>Tote to a 10 dollar unit: Win 28.00; places 17.00, 36.50,</p>
<p>78.50. Dual forecast: 135.00</p>
<p>Hong Kong International Vase, for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over 12 furlongs (2.4 km)</p>
<p>    1. Luso (F.Dettori)    </p>
<p>    2. Royal Snack (D.Oliver)</p>
<p>    3. Privilege (B.Marcus)</p>
<p>14 ran. Winning distances: one and half lengths, two and</p>
<p>three quarter lengths.</p>
<p>Winner trained at Newmarket in England by Clive Brittain and</p>
<p>owned by Saeed Manana.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: $450, 000</p>
<p>Tote: 31.00; places 16.00, 40.50, 36.00. Dual forecast:</p>
<p>247.00</p>
<p>Hong Kong International Bowl, for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over seven furlongs (1.4 km)</p>
<p>    1. Monopolize (D.Beadman) </p>
<p>    2. Dojima Muteki (Y.Muramoto)</p>
<p>    3. Michael's Choice (E.Legrix)</p>
<p>13 ran. Winning distances: short head, one length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by N.Begg and partners syndicate, trained in</p>
<p>Australia by Grahame Begg.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: $450,000</p>
<p>Tote: 60.50; places 21.00, 33.00, 17.00. Dual forecast</p>
<p>344.00</p>
</text>
